# The joint certificate: data part 2

Blocks of the lookup tables encoding the joint table `𝖸` of the joint certificate. At each level
`q`, the pairs `(r, k)` with `𝖸_q(r, k) ≠ 0` are listed in increasing order of the key
`r̃ 2^13 + k`; the block `b` holds the entries `256 b` to `256 b + 255` of that list, the keys as
`32`-bit lanes and the values as `64`-bit lanes.

